# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data
# 6.4 GB of ECMWF GRIBs, IMD NetCDFs, ERA5 forcing and derived arrays.  Most of
# it stays out.  The CNN downscaling training data, benchmark and predictions
# ARE committed (through Git LFS, see .gitattributes) -- allowed only because
# this repo is PRIVATE: IMD and ECMWF data are redistributable only from the
# original providers, so never make the repo public while these files are in
# its history.  README explains how to rebuild everything from source.
data/*
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
# training data: the member archive, the aligned targets, the packed file
!data/processed/s2s/
!data/processed/downscaling_v2_full.npz
!data/processed/percell_v2_full.npz
# EC / EC-QM benchmark and CNN test predictions, fixed split
!data/processed/ec_qm_v2_fixed.npz
!data/processed/percell_v2_fixed.npz
!data/processed/percell_v2_fixed_pw_*.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- third party
# VIC 5.0.1 source tree + compiled arm64 binary.  Upstream is
# https://github.com/UW-Hydro/VIC (GPL-2.0); vendoring a copy here would add a
# licence obligation for no benefit.  Build it from upstream instead.
hydrology/vic/VIC/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- papers
# The source papers are NOT redistributed.  Dong et al. (HESS) is open access
# under CC BY 4.0, but Ambika et al. (GRL) is not, and mixed licences in one
# directory invite mistakes.  Both are cited by DOI in the README.
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- artefacts
# .gitignore does NOT support trailing comments -- "archive/  # note" makes the
# comment part of the pattern and matches nothing.  Keep comments on their own line.

# superseded code and docs, kept locally for provenance
archive/
# trained weights, regenerable -- except the Dong-spec CNN runs, kept (LFS)
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/percell_v2_fixed/
!checkpoints/percell_v2_fixed_pw_*/
# run logs
logs/
.probe_log/
# calibration and repair backups
*.bak_*
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- os / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- credentials
# Belt and braces: these live in ~/.kaggle, never in the project.
kaggle.json
access_token
.env
*.pem
*.key
